# (issue #451) against the deployed set after this PR's bumps: cadvisor
# v0.52.1, alloy v1.18.1, grafana 13.0.6-ubuntu, loki 3.7.6, node-exporter
# v1.12.1 and redis_exporter v1.87.0. The prometheus v3.14.0 and alertmanager
# v0.34.0 bumps clear it from both; promtail is no longer deployed (replaced
# by alloy, phase-825).
# Why no fix (third-party): pinned tags that compile x/net transitively;
# fixing requires an upstream rebuild, and none has shipped.
# ⚠ NOT TRUE OF ja4proxy:2.0.0 — that is a Go stdlib finding
# (deploy/docker/Dockerfile.go-proxy pins golang:1.26.5-alpine) and Go 1.26.6
# fixes it. This waiver must NOT be read as covering our own image; the bump
# is tracked as its own phase, together with splitting .trivyignore into
# first-party and third-party files so a sidecar waiver can never again
# silently suppress a finding in the product.
# Why not exploitable (third-party only): dns/dnsmessage parses
# host-originated DNS records, which none of those components reach in our
# deployment. Re-review at expiry.
CVE-2026-46600 exp:2026-08-23

