# ── Go 1.26.5 stdlib batch, surfaced by a Trivy DB update on 2026-08-15 ──
# Six stdlib CVEs (encoding/asn1 DoS and siblings), all present in
# `stdlib v1.26.5`.
# Carrier set re-measured 2026-08-19 (issue #451). The previous text named
# prometheus:v3.13.2 and alertmanager:v0.33.1; the bumps in this PR
# (v3.14.0 / v0.34.0) CLEAR all six from both images. The real remaining set
# is cadvisor v0.52.1, alloy v1.18.1, grafana 13.0.6-ubuntu, loki 3.7.6,
# node-exporter v1.12.1 and redis_exporter v1.87.0.
# Why no fix HERE: all six are fixed in Go 1.26.6, but these are pinned
# upstream tags we cannot rebuild — the fix only reaches us when each project
# publishes an image built on 1.26.6. Registry re-checked 2026-08-19: every one
# of the six is already on its newest published tag.
# ⚠ NOT waived for our own images. The identical CVEs were present in
# ja4proxy:2.0.0 and Phase 822 FIXED them by bumping the builder to
# golang:1.26.6-alpine; that image now scans clean with no ignorefile at all.
# This is exactly the split this file exists to enforce — see the header.
# Why not exploitable here: these are DoS/parsing bugs in asn1 and related
# stdlib paths. All four components are internal-only scrape targets on the
# monitoring network with no host port exposure; none parses attacker-supplied
# ASN.1 or terminates TLS from an untrusted peer.
# Re-review at expiry: check for upstream rebuilds on Go 1.26.6.
CVE-2026-33818 exp:2026-08-24
CVE-2026-56853 exp:2026-08-24
CVE-2026-56858 exp:2026-08-24
CVE-2026-56859 exp:2026-08-24
CVE-2026-56860 exp:2026-08-24
CVE-2026-56862 exp:2026-08-24

# CVE-2026-71556: Go stdlib finding in grafana/alloy v1.18.1.
# phase-825 introduced Alloy as the supported replacement for the EOL
# grafana/promtail (29 HIGH/CRITICAL -> 6). Five of Alloy's six are already
# waived here for other images; this is the only new one.
# Why no fix: alloy v1.18.1 is the newest published tag (checked 2026-08-17);
# the fix requires an upstream rebuild on a newer Go toolchain and no such tag
# exists. This is a pinned third-party image we cannot rebuild.
# ⚠ Not applicable to our own images — they build on golang:1.26.6-alpine
# (phase-822) and scan clean with no ignorefile.
# Why not exploitable: Alloy is an internal-only log shipper on the monitoring
# network with no host port published. It reads container logs and the proxy's
# own log files and writes to Loki; it terminates no TLS from an untrusted peer
# and parses no attacker-supplied input beyond log lines it forwards verbatim.
# Re-review at expiry: check for an alloy tag built on Go 1.26.6+.
CVE-2026-71556 exp:2026-08-24

# CVE-2026-56864 / CVE-2026-56865: golang.org/x/mod v0.37.0 in grafana/alloy
# v1.18.1 and prom/alertmanager v0.34.0.
#
# Added 2026-08-19 (issue #451). These were NOT in the vuln DB when the
# 2026-08-18 renewal was reviewed, so the ignorefile silently developed a
# two-entry GAP and `make scan-images` began failing on alloy — an image nobody
# had changed. Recorded here because "the file was complete yesterday" is not a
# property that survives a database refresh, and this is the second time a
# renewal review has been overtaken by one.
#
# Why no fix: fixed in golang.org/x/mod 0.40.0, but both are pinned third-party
# images we cannot rebuild. alloy v1.18.1 and alertmanager v0.34.0 are each the
# newest published tag (registry checked 2026-08-19), so no upstream rebuild
# carrying the fix exists yet.
# ⚠ Not applicable to our own images: ja4proxy:2.0.0 scans clean with no
# ignorefile at all (phase-822 golang:1.26.6-alpine builder).
#
# Why not exploitable here: both are attacks by a malicious GOSUMDB / GOPROXY
# against a Go client that is FETCHING MODULES. Neither alloy nor alertmanager
# fetches Go modules at runtime — they are compiled binaries running as
# internal-only services on the monitoring network with no host port published.
# The vulnerable code path is build-time tooling that is never invoked in the
# running container.
# Re-review at expiry: check for alloy / alertmanager tags built against
# golang.org/x/mod >= 0.40.0.
CVE-2026-56864 exp:2026-08-26
CVE-2026-56865 exp:2026-08-26
